q07.

`web/src/connect.ts`

This file is the single place where the ConnectRPC transport and all service clients are constructed. It creates the main transport via `createConnectTransport` (with `window.location.origin` as the base URL, binary format, a credentialed fetch, and an auth interceptor), then exports one client per service with `createClient` — `instanceServiceClient`, `authServiceClient`, `userServiceClient`, `memoServiceClient`, `attachmentServiceClient`, `aiServiceClient`, `shortcutServiceClient`, and `identityProviderServiceClient`.

```184:203:web/src/connect.ts
const transport = createConnectTransport({
  baseUrl: window.location.origin,
  useBinaryFormat: true,
  fetch: fetchWithCredentials,
  interceptors: [authInterceptor],
});

// Core service clients
export const instanceServiceClient = createClient(InstanceService, transport);
export const authServiceClient = createClient(AuthService, transport);
export const userServiceClient = createClient(UserService, transport);
// ... remaining content and configuration clients ...
export const identityProviderServiceClient = createClient(IdentityProviderService, transport);
```

It also creates a separate `refreshTransport` and `refreshAuthClient` (around lines 65–72) used for token refresh, so that refresh calls bypass the auth interceptor.
